{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790485710,"nonce":"WqZiT7Th7fpeM/8v+lEX9FrqYAQ=","title":"Compiler: the inliner's has-calls verdict on a callee depends on processing order","message":"On raytrace-simple, the base build (cbbca5f6) inlines Point$new into Point$__add__ (\"callee has calls: false\"), while a build that only adds library functions and changes unrelated lowering (P-num-arith, a20058a9 and earlier) refuses it (\"callee with calls outside a loop\"; Point$new allocates). Nothing in Point$new or Point$__add__ changed between the two, so whether the callee counts as call-bearing depends on the order the inliner visits functions, not on the callee. raytrace-simple runs slower beyond the spread on the NUC with the refusal.\n\nReproduce: stage raytrace-simple.py with the shims (util.py, optparse.py) and run `ZYNTAX_TRACE_INLINE=1 zypy run raytrace-simple.py -n 1` on both builds; diff the sorted `[inline] Point$__add__` lines.\n\nExpected: one verdict per callee regardless of visit order (decide on the callee as it stands before or after its own inlining, consistently).","files":null}]}